  "notes": [
    "ADR-054-001: component (c) of binding hash is sha256(canonical_uri(resource_uri)). When the auditor presents a resource_uri distinct from the one bound in the signed receipt, the recomputed hash diverges at component (c).",
    "Adversarial scenario: agent or auditor suspects the merchant served a different resource than the one declared in paymentRequirements.resource. The envelope JWS signature remains valid (kid + signature intact), but the binding does NOT semantically tie payment to the actually-served URI.",
    "Test runner MUST recompute the canonical binding hash from inputs.*_declared (using verification_inputs.resource_uri for component c) and assert hash != binding_hash_declared.",
    "binding_hash_declared placeholder is informational — implementations compute the real value dynamically from the canonical 5-component pipeline."
